        "original_id": "fc840950-e7cc-5dbf-a0cf-2829187de229",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jane Mayer, Charles Koch, David Koch, the Koch family\n- Organizations: Koch Industries, Citizens United\n- Products: Dark Money\n- Concepts: conservative libertarians, political influence, nonprofit organizations\n\nFacts:\n- In 1988, Citizens United was started in the United States as a conservative 501(c)(4) non-profit organization with major funding from the billionaire Koch family.\n- In 2013, Koch Industries had revenues of $115 billion and was the second-largest privately owned company in the United States.\n- The Koch family is an American family engaged in business, noted for political activities and control of Koch Industries.\n- In 2016, Jane Mayer published the non-fiction book Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right.\n- Dark Money describes a network of extremely wealthy conservative libertarians, especially Charles Koch and David Koch.\n- Dark Money says Charles Koch, David Koch, and allied organizations worked in tandem to influence academic institutions, think tanks, the courts, statehouses, Congress, and the American presidency for their own benefit.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
